Algorithm for ExtractMax

Step 1: Check if the heap is empty; if it is empty return -1.
Step 2: Store the value at the root because it is the maximum element of the Max Heap.
Step 3: Take the last element of the heap and place it at the root position.
Step 4: Remove the last element from the heap to reduce the heap size.
Step 5: Starting from the last non-leaf node, apply the heapify process to restore the Max Heap property.
Step 6: Continue heapifying until the heap structure becomes valid again.
Step 7: Return the stored maximum element.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)

Algorithm for Heapify

Step 1: Consider a node position in the heap.
Step 2: Find the positions of its left and right children.
Step 3: Compare the value of the current node with its children.
Step 4: Identify the position that contains the largest value among them.
Step 5: If one of the children is larger than the current node, swap their positions.
Step 6: After swapping, apply the heapify process again on the affected child position.
Step 7: Repeat this process until the Max Heap property is satisfied.

Time Complexity: O(log n)
Space Complexity: O(1)



